# Next.js (netmifi-pro)

This App Router / Next.js major may differ from older training data. Prefer
`node_modules/next/dist/docs/` (and current `next` types) over memory.

## Routing

- File-based routes under `app/` only — no `pages/`
- Use `layout.tsx`, `page.tsx`, `loading.tsx`, `error.tsx`, `not-found.tsx` as appropriate
- Typed route helpers from this Next.js version (e.g. `LayoutProps`) — do not invent old `pages` APIs

## Data

- Server Components for reads by default
- Server Actions or Route Handlers (`app/api/.../route.ts`) for mutations
- Cache and revalidate using this version’s APIs; do not copy `getServerSideProps` / `getStaticProps`

## Client boundaries

- `"use client"` at the leaf that needs the browser, not on entire pages
- Do not import server-only modules (`lib` secrets, `fs`, etc.) into client files

## Images and fonts

- `next/image` and `next/font` as in the current docs
- Static files in `public/`

## Config

- App config in `next.config.ts`
- Do not add Pages Router or custom `src/pages` without an explicit decision
